l spending reignited fears that tech firms will take on more debt to finance AI infrastructure. Other hyperscalers also declined, with Alphabet (-3.2%), Microsoft (-2.2%) and Amazon (-4.6%) falling ahead of their earnings reports next week. Tesla dropped 3.1% after scaling back its spending plans, with capital investment in the previous quarter coming in below expectations. Lam Research tumbled 11.8% after issuing a disappointing outlook. Among chipmakers, Nvidia lost 4.4%, Micron shed 6.3%, AMD plunged 8.1%, and Intel fell 8%.\nUnited States Stock Market Index - Stats\nThe main stock market index of United States, the US500, fell to 7666 points on October 22, 2026, losing 1.17% from the previous session. Over the past month, the index has declined 0.51%, though it remains 13.77% higher than a year ago, according to trading on a contract for difference (CFD) that tracks this benchmark index from United States.  Historically, the United States Stock Market Index reached an all time high of 7844.67 in October of 2026. United States Stock Market Index - data, forecasts, historical chart - was last updated on  October 22 of 2026.\nUnited States Stock Market Index - Forecast\nThe main stock market index of United States, the US500, fell to 7666 points on October 22, 2026, losing 1.17% from the previous session. Over the past month, the index has declined 0.51%, though it remains 13.77% higher than a year ago, according to trading on a contract for difference (CFD) that tracks this benchmark index from United States. The United States Stock Market Index is expected to trade at 7524.77 points by the end of this quarter, according to Trading Economics global macro models and analysts expectations. Looking forward, we estimate it to trade at 7032.90 in 12 months time.\nIndexes\nPrice\nDay\nMonth\nYear\nDate\nUS30\n52,863.03\n0.05\n0.0001%\n2.62%\n13.11%\nOct/22\nUS400\n3,636.94\n-29.01\n-0.79%\n-0.43%\n10.89%\nOct/22\nUS2000\n2,783.16\n0.94\n0.03%\n-1.96%\n12.10%\nOct/22\nUS