80%\nYTD\n13.79%\n1Y\n17.71%\n5Y\n833.78%\nAll\n484,951.46%\nBaseline\nAdvanced Chart\nAlphaSpace Chart\nLoading chart for NVDA\nPrevious Close\n221.97\nOpen\n217.23\nBid\n212.00 x 100\nAsk\n223.75 x 100\nDay's Range\n211.26 - 218.88\n52 Week Range\n164.27 - 243.37\nVolume\n121,609,814\nAvg. Volume\n117,416,487\nMarket Cap (intraday)\n5.124T\nBeta (5Y Monthly)\n2.22\nPE Ratio (TTM)\n26.83\nEPS (TTM)\n7.91\nEarnings Date\nNov 17, 2026\nForward Dividend & Yield\n1.00 (0.45%)\n1y Target Est\n328.72\nYahoo Finance Rating\nRating available with Stock Picks access\nNVIDIA Corporation Overview\nSemiconductors / Technology\nNVIDIA Corporation operates as a data center scale AI infrastructure company in the United States, Taiwan, China, Hong Kong, Europe, and internationally. It operates through Compute & Networking, and Graphics segments. The Compute & Networking segment provides data center accelerated computing and networking platforms and artificial intelligence solutions and software, and automotive platforms and autonomous and electric vehicle solutions, including software. The Graphics segment offers GeForce GPUs for gaming and PCs; Quadro/NVIDIA RTX GPUs for enterprise workstation graphics. The company's products are used in gaming, professional visualization, data center, and automotive markets. It sells its products to original equipment manufacturers, original device manufacturers, system integrators and distributors, independent software vendors, cloud service providers, add-in board manufacturers, distributors, automotive manufacturers and tier-1 automotive suppliers, and other ecosystem participants. It has a collaboration with Cisco to develop Ultra-Dense Small Form Factor Pluggable (USFP), a high-density optical module pluggable transceiver. It has a collaboration with ChipAgents to develop Build-A-Chip-Bench, a benchmark for AI agents carrying chip design tasks and The Company has a strategic alliance with MediaTek to build the next generations of AI computing platforms. NVIDIA Corporation was incorporated in 1993 and is headquartered in Santa Clara, California.\nwww.nvidia.com\n42,000\nFull Time Employees\nJanuary 25\nFiscal Year Ends\nTechnology\nSector\nSemiconductors\nIndustry\nMore about NVIDIA Corporation\nRecent News\nView More\nAll\nNews\nEarnings Calls\nPress Releases\nSEC Filings\nView More\nPerformance Overview\nTrailing total returns as of 10/22/2026, which may include dividends or other distributions.\nBenchmark is\nS&P 500 (^GSPC)\n.\nYTD Return\nNVDA\n14.05%\nS&P 500 (^GSPC)\n11.95%\n1-Year Return\nNVDA\n17.99%\nS&P 500 (^GSPC)\n14.39%\n3-Year Return\nNVDA\n414.28%\nS&P 500 (^GSPC)\n81.42%\n5-Year Return\nNVDA\n837.89%\nS&P 500 (^GSPC)\n68.62%\nEarnings Trends\nView More\nEarnings Per Share\ngaap\nGAAP\nnongaap\nNormalized\ngaap\nGAAP\nnongaap\nNormalized\nRevenue vs. Earnings\nyearly\nAnnual\nquarterly\nQuarterly\nyearly\nAnnual\nquarterly\nQuarterly\nQ2 FY27\nRevenue\n96.22B\nEarnings\n59.69B\nProfit Margin\n62.03%\nQ3\nFY26\nQ4\nFY26\nQ1\nFY27\nQ2\nFY27\n0\n20B\n40B\n60B\n80B\n60.0%\n65.0%\n70.0%\nView More\nAnalyst Insights\nView More\nAnalyst Price Targets\n180.00\n328.72\nAverage\n212.21\nCurrent\n515.00\nHigh\nAnalyst Recommendations\nStrong Buy\nBuy\nHold\nUnderperform\nSell\nLatest Rating\nDate\n10/22/2026\nAnalyst\nNeedham\nRating Action\nReiterates\nRating\nBuy\nPrice Action\nMaintains\nPrice Target\n300 ->  300\nView More\nStatistics\nView More\nValuation Measures\nMarket Cap\nEnterprise Value\nTrailing P/E\nForward P/E\nPEG Ratio (5yr expected)\nPrice/Sales  (ttm)\nPrice/Book  (mrq)\nEnterprise Value/Revenue\nEnterprise Value/EBITDA\nFinancial Highlights\nProfitability and Income Statement\nProfit Margin\n63.66%\nReturn on Assets  (ttm)\n53.57%\nReturn on Equity  (ttm)\n117.21%\nRevenue  (ttm)\n302.97B\nNet Income Avi to Common  (ttm)\n192.88B\nDiluted EPS  (ttm)\n7.91\nBalance Sheet and Cash Flow\nTotal Cash  (mrq)\n62.47B\nTotal Debt/Equity  (mrq)\n16.97%\nLevered Free Cash Flow  (ttm)\n41